  "result": "Perfect! The bulk discount feature is working correctly. Let me create a summary:\n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation Summary\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n**In `src/totals.js`, updated `invoiceTotals()` function:**\n- Lines with **qty \u2265 10** get an extra **2.5% bulk discount**\n- Bulk discount is applied **after** the line discount (tier or explicit)\n- VAT is calculated on the amount **after both discounts**\n- The bulk discount is included in the `discount` field of the return value\n\n### How It Works\n\n**Calculation order:**\n1. Line total = qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n2. Line discount = lineTotal \u00d7 (discountPercent) / 100\n3. Amount after line discount = lineTotal - lineDiscount\n4. If qty \u2265 10: bulkDiscount = (amount after line discount) \u00d7 2.5 / 100\n5. Total discount = lineDiscount + bulkDiscount\n6. VAT = roundCents((lineTotal - total discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100)\n7. Total = subtotal - total discount + VAT - voucher (clamped at 0)\n\n### Test Coverage\n\n**16 new bulk discount tests** in `test/totals.test.js`:\n- \u2705 Bulk discount applies at qty = 10\n- \u2705 Bulk discount does not apply at qty = 9\n- \u2705 Bulk discount applies after line discount\n- \u2705 Works with tier discounts\n- \u2705 Works with multiple lines\n- \u2705 Works with different VAT rates\n- \u2705 Works with vouchers\n- \u2705 Boundary cases (9 units, 10 units, 11 units)\n- \u2705 Large quantities (1000+)\n- \u2705 Rounding edge cases\n- \u2705 Precision handling\n\n**All 389 tests passing** \u2713",
